      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The approach focusing on systemic injustices and power struggles is actually more effective for middle schoolers because it fosters critical thinking and prepares them to navigate a complex, real-world society. Sticking solely to national triumphs and shared values often feels hollow to teenagers who are already questioning authority and seeking authenticity. By teaching the truth about power dynamics and historical inequities, we equip students with the empathy and analytical skills they desperately need to become engaged, responsible citizens.",
